    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_57d358d43b92c393db9fc4b5e5cc18d45557d4cb4766a5e88797f15b1d08c577",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "For Gaussian increments with drift theta and unit variance, the first ladder height is reorganized from a separate expectation at each positive drift into the local analytic germ theta -> E_theta S_tau at zero. This representation makes Taylor coefficients, rather than isolated numerical values, the objects to determine and places the stopping-time problem in the same analytic setting as the recalled continuation of zeta. It gains access to local coefficient structure but does not itself supply the continuation argument or a coefficient identity with zeta; those remain proof obligations beyond this exact span, and the Gaussian/unit-variance assumption matters.",
