    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b666f6825a569257470769bf8eb27a74cee31a8c71510f3271426091a4fa347c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A single parameterized analytic family supplies several probabilistic readouts: its alpha=1/2 specialization gives the ladder-height expansion and limiting-overshoot coefficient, likelihood and renewal identities transport that expansion to remote-boundary crossing probabilities, and other alpha values plus transform matching yield higher ladder-height moments and derivatives of the limiting overshoot. The outputs are related projections of the family, not all instances of one unchanged scalar series.",
