    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c4b8dd2781e77635123f60e6372f81bd490d5119333fe28188f3304da5a2b378",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source turns the positive-drift ladder-height expectation into a zeta-coefficient engine by a concrete chain: a fluctuation identity and Wald's equation reduce its logarithmic derivative to an exponentially damped Dirichlet series, singular-term subtraction makes that series analytic at the boundary, and Taylor-coefficient recovery supplies the zeta values that reconstruct the original expectation by integration and exponentiation.",
